<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pekan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pekan is the royal town of the Malaysian state of Pahang, near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pahang-river">Pahang River</a> on the east coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>. It was the seat of the first sultans of Pahang from around 1470 and later of the Bendahara rulers and the modern sultans, whose palace stands there. It is also the burial place of the Pahang royal family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pekan.jpg" alt="Pekan" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Slleong · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pekan_13.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
